      <data key="d7">["161050", "63780"]</data>
      <data key="d8">["In voice applications, this means I end up using a pipeline that includes speech-to-text ( STT, also known as ASR, or automatic speech recognition) to transcribe the user’ s words, then processes the text using one or more LLM calls, and finally returns an audio response to the user via TTS ( text-to-speech).", "Today, most production-grade voice systems generally follow a three-part architecture: ( 1) a speech-to-text ( STT) model, ( 2) a large language model ( LLM), and ( 3) a text-to-speech ( TTS) model."]</data>
