      <data key="d8">["Well, intuitively this sounds reasonable, yet some recent careful research shows the opposite – the paper Context Length Alone Hurts LLM Performance Despite Perfect Retrieval ( https: //aclanthology.org/2025.findings-emnlp.1264.pdf) accepted at EMNLP 2025 ( a top AI conference) demonstrated a sobering reality: while models can retrieve a specific needle from a 1M token haystack, their ability to reason over that data collapses."]</data>
