      <data key="d8">["Then weâll introduce practical caching patterns for agentic systems: RAG and retrieval caching ( query â top-k chunks, embeddings, rerank results) tool-result caching ( APIs/DB queries with TTL, idempotency keys, provenance) response + reasoning artifact caching ( answer reuse with âfreshnessâ guards) workflow memoization ( agent step outputs keyed by inputs, policies, and versions) organization-level knowledge reuse ( shared âanswer primitivesâ for FAQs, policies, and ideation) But caching isnât free: it creates complexity around staleness, governance, personalization, and security boundaries."]</data>
