      <data key="d8">["The denier, a volunteer working, on the project named Scott Shambaugh, later wrote that matplotlib is in the midst of âa surge in low quality contributions enabled by coding agents.â This problem, according to Shambaugh, has âaccelerated with the release of OpenClaw and the moltbook platform, a system by which âpeople give AI agents initial personalities and let them loose to run on their computers and across the internet with free rein and little oversight.â After Shambaugh snubbed the agent, Â a post appeared on a blog called “ MJ Rathbun | Scientific Coder ð¦.â The title was âGatekeeping in Open Source: The Scott Shambaugh Story.â The apparently AI-written article, which includes cliches like âLet that sink in, â constructed a fairly unconvincing argument in the voice of someone indignant about various slights and injustices."]</data>
      <data key="d9">same_sentence_entity_cooccurrence</data>
    </edge>
