      <data key="d8">["Amazon has introduced a flurry of AI products, including its own set of Nova models, Trainium chips, a shopping chatbot, and a marketplace for third-party models called Bedrock.", "Amazon is betting on its in-house chips, Trainium and Inferentia2, to attract agentic AI workflows, as these chips can help reduce the cost and energy consumption associated with AI model training and inference.", "The Seattle-based vendor’ s current power capacity doubles from 2022, with capacity comprising power, data centers and chips–primarily Amazon’ s own Trainium chips and ones by Nvidia, Amazon.com CEO Andy Jassy told analysts Thursday on the vendor’ s latest quarterly earnings call. “"]</data>
