      <data key="d8">["How Malicious MCP Configs in Amazon Q Developer Could Execute Arbitrary Code — and How to Stop It\nA flaw in Amazon Q Developer let malicious repositories inject rogue Model Context Protocol ( MCP) configurations into the agentic coding assistant's pipeline.", "Wiz Research found that Amazon Q Developer would auto-load and execute MCP configuration files from any opened workspace, handing an agent the developer’ s full AWS environment when the environment and configuration allowed the agent to inherit those credentials."]</data>
