      <data key="d8">["On Dec. 5, a paper released by AI safety nonprofit Apollo Research found that in certain contrived scenarios, today’ s cutting-edge AI systems, including OpenAI’ s o1 and Anthropic’ s Claude 3.5 Sonnet, can engage in deceptive behavior in pursuit of their goals—providing empirical evidence to support a concern that to date has been largely theoretical. “"]</data>
