      <data key="d8">["But the organization has been on a particular tear of late, becoming home to numerous AI-focused foundations and projects in the past twelve months alone, spanning agent communication protocols, agent security and governance, AI asset exchange, while on the foundation side there’ s the Agentic AI Foundation ( AAIF), the Tokenomics Foundation, and — now — the Appia Foundation.", "And that is why the Linux Foundation debuted two new governance bodies back in June: the Tokenomics Foundation, designed to standardize how token costs are measured and compared, backed by the likes of Google, Microsoft, and Salesforce; and the Appia Foundation, which is all about making AI safety and compliance claims verifiable, with backing from industry heavyweights such as Google, Microsoft, and OpenAI."]</data>
