      <data key="d8">["A recent IDC report highlighted how for product managers, investing more in engineering and research and development ( R &amp; D) correlates with lower cost of goods sold ( COGS) and higher revenue growth for manufacturers, suggesting that investments in product engineering investments drive financial success.1 As product complexity and connectivity has continued to increase, engineers’ roles have become multi-disciplinary, requiring interaction with various data sources and tools, such as product lifecycle management ( PLM), computer-aided design ( CAD), computer-aided manufacturing ( CAM), application lifecycle management ( ALM) for software requirements, and computer-aided engineering ( CAE)."]</data>
