      <data key="d5">cooccurrence</data>
      <data key="d6">2</data>
      <data key="d7">["140386", "140423"]</data>
      <data key="d8">["By the time that GPT-4 came along in November 2022 and sparked the GenAI Boom, the model was closed source, and to help sell its iron, Cerebras created a turbocharged version of the open source GPT-3 models that could run on its CS-1 and CS-2 systems – including model architecture, training data, model weights, and checkpoints under an Apache 2.0 license.", "As far as we can tell from the S-1 reports that Cerebras has filed in September 2024 and then again this week as it has a second go at going IPO, G42 has spent $ 434.5 million on Cerebras gear and support for its cloud buildout of a mix of CS-2 and CS-3 waferscale systems from 2023 through 2025, representing 49.4 percent of revenues for Cerebras for those years."]</data>
      <data key="d9">same_sentence_entity_cooccurrence</data>
    </edge>
