      <data key="d8">["The company started out in 1993 as a GPU maker, and for more than a decade has led the charge to the top of the AI heap with those chips firmly in hand Nvidia’ s CUDA computing platform and programming model opened the door for the GPUs to move beyond its graphics rendering roots and into general-purpose computing in the datacenter, the NVLink interconnect enabled fast communication directly between GPUs, and newer software innovations like Dynamo – an open, distributed inference framework – all play key roles in Nvidia’ s platform push, but it’ s the compute complexes like Grace Blackwell today and the upcoming Vera-Rubin compute complex slated for later this year – and eventually the follow-on to that, the Vera-Feynman platform – that gets people jazzed."]</data>
