      <data key="d8">["A so-called `` reasoning model, '' DeepSeek-R1 is a digital assistant that performs as well as OpenAI’ s o1 on certain AI benchmarks for math and coding tasks, was trained with far fewer chips and is approximately 96% cheaper to use, according to the company. “", "About a week ago, DeepSeek, a company based in China, released DeepSeek-R1, a remarkable model whose performance on benchmarks is comparable to OpenAI’ s o1.", "DeepSeek’ s open-source models that were released last week, DeepSeek-R1-Zero and DeepSeek-R1, showed similar performance to that of OpenAI’ s reasoning models and Meta Platforms’ Llama models on leading benchmarks, such as the AIME 2024."]</data>
