      <data key="d8">["At the core of how Google plans to give agents access to websites and the tools they provide is WebMCP, the emerging open standard for exposing JavaScript functions and HTML forms, for example, to agents. “", "Why WebMCP Is the Most Important Thing Google Announced at I/O 2026 ( And Nobody's Talking About It)\nI was watching the Google I/O 2026 Developer Keynote on my laptop at 11:30 PM with a cup of cold chai.", "While Google was careful to note that WebMCP is still experimental and not yet widely supported, its promotion at I/O indicates that agent-native protocols for web development will soon be commonplace."]</data>
