      <data key="d8">["Nvidia paid $ 20 billion for Groq’ s IP and key talent — including founder Jonathan Ross, who created Google’ s TPUs — in what they called a “ non-exclusive licensing agreement. ”", "This is one reason why Nvidia essentially bought Groq on Christmas Eve 2025 through an “ aquihire ” deal licensing the company’ s Learning Processing Unit technology and hiring most of its key engineering people, including co-founder Jonathan Ross and chief operating officer Sunny Madra, for $ 20 billion. (", "In 2026, we are seeing the mainstream adoption of “ AI PCs ” and “ Inference Servers ” powered by next-generation silicon from NVIDIA, Apple ( M5 series), and specialized fast-growing AI startups like Groq."]</data>
