      <data key="d8">["Nutanix is formally extending support for external storage systems — marking an evolution from its traditional all-in-one HCI stack.", "Nutanix itself has evolved considerably since 2011, when it launched as a provider of hyper-converged infrastructure ( HCI), with its Acropolis Operating System ( AOS) platform and virtual machine ( VM) hypervisor — Acropolis Hypervisor AHV — providing users with a one-stop shop for scalable, storage-backed infrastructure.", "NKP Metal represents an extension of the Nutanix operating model and HCI stack to bare-metal Kubernetes environments, enabling organizations to run containers directly on physical infrastructure while maintaining a consistent level of automation, lifecycle management, networking, and enterprise data services they rely on in virtualized environments."]</data>
