      <data key="d8">["Nvidia paid $ 20 billion for Groq’ s IP and key talent — including founder Jonathan Ross, who created Google’ s TPUs — in what they called a “ non-exclusive licensing agreement. ”", "This is one reason why Nvidia essentially bought Groq on Christmas Eve 2025 through an “ aquihire ” deal licensing the company’ s Learning Processing Unit technology and hiring most of its key engineering people, including co-founder Jonathan Ross and chief operating officer Sunny Madra, for $ 20 billion. (", "We expected for Nvidia to move fast to deploy the tensor streaming processors created by Jonathan Ross, the ex-Googler who created a fully-scheduled, programmable tensor processing unit after he left the search engine giant."]</data>
