      <data key="d8">["Nvidia’ s ascent from scrappy startup to tech royalty began in 1993 in a Silicon Valley Denny’ s, where Jensen Huang and his friends Chris Malachowsky and Curtis Priem sketched out a vision for a computer chip that could render realistic 3D graphics.", "The session was one of several SCSP panels this week with NVIDIA leaders on stage: Cofounder and NVIDIA Fellow Chris Malachowsky will lead a panel on the AI+ Careers Workforce Task Force; Rev Lebaredian will speak on physical AI and simulation; Dion Harris will discuss AI-accelerated American science and AI infrastructure for Africa; and John Josephakis will join a session on U.S. quantum leadership.", "âWeâre just having a hard time acknowledging that itâs taking away job opportunities.â Nvidia cofounder Chris Malachowsky attempted to use his graduation address at the University of Florida to ease some fears: Forget the ânoise, â he said."]</data>
