      <data key="d8">["Our four hot trends to watch out for in 2024 included what we called customized chatbots—interactive helper apps powered by multimodal large language models ( check: we didn’ t know it yet, but we were talking about what everyone now calls agents, the hottest thing in AI right now); generative video ( check: few technologies have improved so fast in the last 12 months, with OpenAI and Google DeepMind releasing their flagship video generation models, Sora and Veo, within a week of each other this December); and more general-purpose robots that can do a wider range of tasks ( check: the payoffs from large language models continue to trickle down to other parts of the tech industry, and robotics is top of the list)."]</data>
