      <data key="d8">["Led by Joon Sung Park, a Stanford PhD student in computer science, the team recruited 1,000 people who varied by age, gender, race, region, education, and political ideology.", "I think this is probably the most exciting moment ever to be a Stanford PhD student in social sciences, ” said Gentzkow, who is the faculty director of Stanford Impact Labs ( SIL). “", "Joon Sung Park, a Stanford PhD graduate who completed his doctorate advised by Michael Bernstein and Percy Liang, founded Simile after conducting research in which 25 AI agents lived simulated lives in a virtual town called Smallville, holding conversations and forming routines without human scripting."]</data>
