    <edge source="person:jira" target="person:zendesk">
      <data key="d4">MENTIONED_WITH</data>
      <data key="d5">cooccurrence</data>
      <data key="d6">3</data>
      <data key="d7">["148317", "151250", "42014"]</data>
      <data key="d8">["It’ s worth noting that GitLab Duo Agentic Chat also supports the open Model Context Protocol ( MCP), allowing agents to draw extra context from external systems ( e.g. Jira, ServiceNow, or ZenDesk) and, where supported, take actions within those tools directly from the chat interface.", "The API Battleground: A New Era of Platform Wars\nAs an investor who’ s met hundreds of B2B AI startups, I can tell you with confidence that one trend is crystal clear: modern AI products almost always depend on incumbents’ data, accessed via APIs — Slack, Salesforce, Zendesk, QuickBooks, Jira, LinkedIn and beyond.", "Instead of letting an agent query across Salesforce, Zendesk, Jira, and Slack at runtime, the Context Store pulls those systems together ahead of time into a single index that preserves entity history and current state."]</data>
      <data key="d9">same_sentence_entity_cooccurrence</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="person:jira" target="protocol:model-context-protocol">
      <data key="d4">MENTIONED_WITH</data>
      <data key="d5">cooccurrence</data>
      <data key="d6">5</data>
      <data key="d7">["113245", "148442", "151250", "49695", "64899"]</data>
      <data key="d8">["It’ s worth noting that GitLab Duo Agentic Chat also supports the open Model Context Protocol ( MCP), allowing agents to draw extra context from external systems ( e.g. Jira, ServiceNow, or ZenDesk) and, where supported, take actions within those tools directly from the chat interface.", "MCP shines when your work touches multiple systems like GitHub, Slack, and Jira without you stitching it together.", "I had three MCP servers running: mcp-atlassian for Jira and Confluence, chrome-devtools for browser automation, and context7 for documentation lookups."]</data>
      <data key="d9">same_sentence_entity_cooccurrence</data>
    </edge>
